Bot-only groups dissolve themselves: when the last real player walks out
of (or logs off from) a raid or party made with bots, the group's bot leader
disbands it on the next manager pass and every bot goes back to the pool.

Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.{h,cpp}
         (new DisbandBotOnlyGroups, called from UpdateAIInternal)
         includes CharacterCache.h
No tracked src/server/ files change -- no core diff in this record; it
documents gitignored module edits.

Why: report #157 -- "leaving a group with bots doesn't seem to disband the
group and return them to the pool to be used, at least for raids".

Root cause: the per-bot "leave group if the leader is a random bot" cleanup
lives in ProcessBot(Player*), but ProcessBot(uint32) early-returns for
grouped bots BEFORE ever reaching it -- so once a bot joined a group, that
cleanup was unreachable for it. The only other check (groupValid in
OnBotLogin) runs when a bot logs IN, so a live bot-only group outlived its
players indefinitely.

The sweep runs each manager pass (30-60s cadence) over online bots and
disbands any non-LFG/BG/BF group whose members are all bots -- mirroring the
login check's groupValid semantics (real player present keeps it; a member
on a real account keeps it when PlayerbotAIConfig.KeepAltsInGroup is set).
Only the leader bot issues the disband, so one packet frees the whole raid.
LFG groups are left to the dungeon finder, BG/BF raids to their systems.
